{"availability":"available","full":"daniserrano7/jira-clone","name":"jira-clone","description":"Jira-inspired project management app with React, TypeScript and Remix: kanban boards, issues and real-time updates.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":96,"forks":30,"created":"2021-12-01T12:23:12Z","updated":"2025-10-25T22:25:40Z","branch":"master","homepage":"https://jira-clone.fly.dev","topics":["kanban","react","remix-run","typescript"],"demo":"https://jira-clone.fly.dev/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T21:24:48.942Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T21:24:48.942Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T21:24:48.942Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T21:24:48.942Z","stars":96,"forks":30}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A simplified Jira clone application with some custom modifications made with Remix Run. This is a personal project for practicing skills and it is not intended to work as a real Jira application. It is still in early development and some features and improves are coming.","For pragmatic purposes, many features are not included. Others have been modified according to my tastes. The application should serve the basic functionalities of a project management software. I have taken inspiration from the actual Jira website, as well as from Trello. Also, Ivor's Jira clone has been a great inspiration for me (I have to admit I like his designs more than Jira's originals). I only took ideas and resources (fonts and icons) from the original projects, all developments have being from scratch and by myself.","The app simulates Jira's workspace, where you can create projects, assign users and create and update issues. It uses a SQLite database to store the data, which can be stored locally on your environment (in the live demo it is placed in the Fly's persistent storage). The content is rendered server-side thanks to Remix Run framework, and it barely uses client stores (only for session data and issues search)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/daniserrano7/jira-clone/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"97774e116ffef28c39f68a8757a8ee0197dd9203e78f5e0f74ec6e8afdc6d0a9","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T21:24:49.069Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T21:24:49.069Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A simplified Jira clone application with some custom modifications made with Remix Run. This is a personal project for practicing skills and it is not intended to work as a real Jira application. It is still in early development and some features and improves are coming.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/daniserrano7/jira-clone/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"It is divided in three main sections: login, projects list and project space.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/daniserrano7/jira-clone/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"The login section is the first one you will see when you open the app.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/daniserrano7/jira-clone/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"97774e116ffef28c39f68a8757a8ee0197dd9203e78f5e0f74ec6e8afdc6d0a9","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/daniserrano7/jira-clone/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T21:24:49.069Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2025-10-25T22:25:40Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/daniserrano7/jira-clone/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T21:24:49.070Z","hash":"97774e116ffef28c39f68a8757a8ee0197dd9203e78f5e0f74ec6e8afdc6d0a9","originalBytes":12575,"storedBytes":12575,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["run","project","following","application","folder","command","database","domain","remix","jira","projects","create","e.g.","execute","login","test","user","app","build","clone","css","entities","infrastructure","npm","other","structure","tailwind","theme","used","which","components","created","find",